# Fork ownership: origin only

This checkout is **seth-wood/gloomberb**, a personal fork. It is not the upstream
`gloom-sh/gloomberb` project workspace for shipping.

## Never do (hard ban)

- Open, update, or close PRs with `--repo gloom-sh/gloomberb` (or any `gloom-sh/*` repo)
- `gh pr create` whose base repo resolves to `gloom-sh/gloomberb`
- Push feature branches to `gloom-sh` remotes
- `git fetch upstream` / `git pull upstream` / rebase or merge `upstream/main`
- Sync fork / "Update from upstream" / reset onto the original upstream `main`
- File issues on `gloom-sh/gloomberb` unless the user explicitly asks for that exact upstream issue

## Always do

- Treat `origin` as `seth-wood/gloomberb` (verify with `git remote -v` if unsure)
- Push with `git push -u origin HEAD`
- Open PRs only against the fork:

```bash
gh pr create --repo seth-wood/gloomberb --head <branch> --base main …
```

  Or omit `--repo` only when `gh` defaults to `seth-wood/gloomberb` from `origin`.
- If a command would touch `gloom-sh/*`, stop and retarget to the fork

## If you already mistargeted upstream

1. Close the upstream PR immediately with a short note that it was opened by mistake.
2. Open the same PR on `seth-wood/gloomberb`.
3. Do not leave an open PR on `gloom-sh/gloomberb`.

If upstream interaction seems required, ask the user first. Default answer is no.
